cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Entity-linkage failure in longitudinal health data: analysis code and
  manuscript
message: >-
  If you use this material, please cite the manuscript. If you use the
  validation method itself, please cite the paneldx software.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Imran
    given-names: Muhammad Umer
    affiliation: School of Medicine, Nanchang University
    email: umer@3dex.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22086703
repository-code: "https://github.com/stemmatics/paneldx-paper"
version: 1.0.3
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, intermediate results and manuscript for a study of
  entity-linkage failure in panel data. A longitudinal dataset asserts that
  rows sharing an identifier describe the same entity observed repeatedly
  over time; where that assertion is false, within-entity analysis is
  invalidated without any error being raised. The study characterises the
  defect, evaluates an automated test across 63 public longitudinal
  datasets, and reports a case study in which the defect suppressed the
  naive baseline that would otherwise have exposed it.
keywords:
  - panel data
  - longitudinal data
  - data leakage
  - entity resolution
  - reproducibility
  - health informatics
